  "vulnerability_information": "I would like to report a case of malicious package (flat-stream) that made it's way into many other npm packages. One such popular package is `event-stream` (user dominictarr transferred the ownership of an npm module to another user because he wasn't actively maintaining it. That user then added malicious dependency to the package)\n\nSee discussion here: \nhttps://github.com/dominictarr/event-stream/issues/116\n\n# Module\n\n**module name:**  flatmap-stream\n**version:** [MODULE VERSION]\n**npm page:** `https://www.npmjs.com/package/flatmap-stream` (removed from npm by now)\n\n## Module Description\n\nIt is not yet clear what the malicious code was doing. \nSee discussion here: https://github.com/dominictarr/event-stream/issues/116#issuecomment-441737695\n\n## Module Stats\n\n> Replace stats below with numbers from npm’s module page:\n\nflatmap-stream is not popular, but event-stream is very popular (1,996,440 downloads per week)\n\n## Impact\n\nRCE",
